I've been receiving comments and other Collatz investigators are sharing their own work with me now. Here's one comments and what I would like us to investigate: "My remaining concern is not so much whether the obstruction has been narrowed, but whether the framework itself is a faithful compression of the full Collatz dynamics.

Tao’s work starts from the behavior of all integers and progressively constrains what is possible. Here the flow feels somewhat reversed: the surviving counterexample profile is being narrowed more and more.

So the question I keep coming back to is:

How do we know that the finite-shadow language captures all arithmetic mechanisms available to Collatz, rather than only the mechanisms available to the surviving candidates inside the shadow framework?

If that faithfulness can be established, the program becomes substantially stronger."